Core request B1, filed by #260 F2 with a driven receipt and reproduced by #260 I,
unenacted since. A ring's authored gap is 2.2px; one-decimal path emission put the
drawn edge at 2.109px because a 0.05 rounding lands on both radii and both endpoints
of a RADIAL edge and the errors do not cancel as a cartesian rect's do.

Local n2 (2 decimals) in dv-render-donut.js, used ONLY for path geometry — pt() and
arc(). data-* attributes keep n1: they are the tip/label contract, not the drawn edge.
The same swap in the two injected AUTO-BEHAVIOUR copies (Chart-donut, Chart-pie), so
gen_component_partials --check is byte-exact for both.

⛔ NOT DONE, both ⬛ Dave's by the #260 carry: GAP stays 2.2 (F2: the 0.2 is the
CARTESIAN budget, an independent mechanism), and the pie's magic 0.35*ro judging
constant is untouched — a pie has no inner edge, so its 2.108 -> 2.134 is a different
thing and this patch does not claim to fix it.

